): NodeParameterValue | INodeParameters | NodeParameterValue[] | INodeParameters[] {",resolveSimpleParameterValue accepts the user-configured workflow expression that supplies the attacker-controlled function name and arguments.,"{""code"":""		data.extend = extend;"",""desc"":""The extend helper is assigned to the sandbox data context here, becoming callable from any user-supplied expression in this scope. This is the exploit chain's origin: extend is exposed with no functionName validation at this boundary, so an attacker may pass any string including 'constructor' as the function name, enabling the downstream path to the Function constructor."",""file"":""packages/workflow/src/expression.ts"",""line"":485}","{""code"":""	resolveSimpleParameterValue(
		parameterValue: NodeParameterValue,
		data: IWorkflowDataProxyData,
